  "query_preview": "..\n\nKEY MESSAGE 1...Chance for rain showers by late next week, \nthough little to no drought improvement anticipated.\n\nKEY MESSAGE 1 DESCRIPTION... A low pressure system to the far \nnorth moves eastward, pushing a front through New England late \nnext week. Ensemble models have slowed the progression of the \nfront with more members leaning towards Thursday evening and \nThursday night for rain. Upper air model soundings indicate a \nlarge dry airmass ahead of the front. This coupled with the \ndecreasing intensity of the front, rain showers look to be \nminimal, especially for the north. Cannot rule out some \nscattered rain showers across the south.",
